# Copy to .env (repo root, gitignored) before running `pnpm docker:prod`.
# Used by docker-compose.prod.yml's cloudflared service.
#
# Get this from the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard: Networks -> Tunnels ->
# your tunnel -> Configure -> copy the token out of the install command
# (the long value after `--token`).
TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# --- Cloudflare Realtime TURN (WebRTC media relay) -------------------------
# Required for proximity voice/video between people on different networks.
# WebRTC media is peer-to-peer UDP and does NOT travel through the Cloudflare
# Tunnel above (which only carries signaling and PocketBase traffic), so
# without a TURN relay any two peers whose NATs can't be hole-punched simply
# never exchange audio or video. Two app instances on one machine always
# worked without it, which is what made this look like a "weird" bug.
#
# Get these from the Cloudflare dashboard: Realtime -> TURN Keys -> create a
# key, then copy the Key ID and the API token. Keep them server-side only;
# they are never sent to clients (the server mints short-lived credentials
# from them and serves those from GET /ice).
TURN_KEY_ID=
TURN_KEY_API_TOKEN=
